WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:02.150
New tech.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.150
An old grudge.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.310
And maybe a fan-service cameo to boot.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.217
There's plenty to parse in the trailer for
the third season of "The Mandalorian".

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:11.360
Grogu, apparently, has a brand new bassinet.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.919
While this might seem a little inconsequential
in the grand scheme of things, what's interesting

00:00:15.919 --> 00:00:19.760
is that it seems to be that this carriage
comes equipped with a few gadgets.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.820
There's a moment in the trailer in which the
titular Mandalorian, Din Djarin, and Grogu

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.820
are moving through what looks like a dark
cave.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.630
A beam of light pops on from the front of
Grogu's crib.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
Maybe Peli Motto has kitted out the floating
pod with some adventuring gear, or perhaps

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.390
Din's been tinkering with it in his spare
time.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.950
And wouldn't you think there are some other
handy hidden features?

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.160
There's also a blink-and-you'll-miss-it shot
of Doctor Pershing and someone else strolling

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.840
through some kind of facility.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.420
Fans will remember that he's the scientist
working on the cloning project for the remains

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.460
of the Empire.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.980
He was last seen being forced by Djarin and
Cara Dune to help break into Gideon's ship.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.870
Considering the Empire wants to use Grogu
for its experiments, it might not be a good

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.390
sign that Pershing is back, but maybe we'll
find out more about what he was up to with

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.673
all those dead clones.

00:01:02.644 --> 00:01:04.834
"Sadly, the body rejected the blood."

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.350
Further into the trailer, there are also some
moody shots of a ruined Mandalorian city.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:14.000
Bo-Katan Kryze stands in a long hallway that
looks very similar to the throne room on Mandalore

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.680
seen in "The Clone Wars."

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.640
That said, it also looks a little bit small
to be the exact same location, unless it's

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.040
gotten a makeover in the last few decades.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.530
It's not impossible that the shot just makes
it look more cramped, or the throne itself

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.500
was moved elsewhere after the Empire purged
the planet.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.885
As for Bo-Katan, it's clear she harbors a
grudge against Din Djarin for a couple of reasons.

00:01:32.885 --> 00:01:38.000
For one, calling out that the Children of
the Watch caused a rift among the Mandalorian population.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.510
Then there's the fact that Din won the Darksaber
from Moff Gideon, something Bo-Katan wanted

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:46.260
to do herself so that she could rightfully
take Mandalore's throne.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:50.801
As Pedro Pascal, who plays Din Djarin, hinted
during an interview with Total Film, Din is

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:54.590
clearly going to become a reluctant leader,
which suggests he might have to fend off an

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.159
attack from Bo-Katan.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:00.479
The trailer shows Din alongside a few other
Mandalorians, each with their own unique helmets

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:01.479
and armor.

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:05.726
Perhaps the reluctant hero will add a few
new members to Clan Mudhorn in Season 3.

00:02:05.806 --> 00:02:10.200
The trailer seemingly reveals a surprising
appearance from a fan-favorite "Star Wars"

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.360
alien: Babu Frik.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.849
It looks like the tiny Anzellan droidsmith
is back after his scene-stealing debut in

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:17.709
"The Rise of Skywalker."

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:21.219
It's worth pointing out that Frik isn't referred
to by name, so it could easily be another

00:02:21.219 --> 00:02:24.010
Anzellan with a talent for fiddling with droids.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.749
The character certainly looks and sounds like
Frik, though.

00:02:26.749 --> 00:02:29.400
And wouldn't it be more fun for it to be him?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.483
"Babu Frik, can you help us with this?"

00:02:37.237 --> 00:02:40.919
It's not clear whether Shirley Henderson,
who is best known for playing Moaning Myrtle

00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:45.708
in the "Harry Potter" films, is reprising
her voice role as Frik, but it's certainly possible.

00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:46.415
Who knows?

00:02:46.415 --> 00:02:49.540
We might even get to learn more about Frik's
mysterious past.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:53.360
Henderson told Esquire that she's thought
of a tragic backstory for the little engineer.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.980
"Beyond the film, Babu has lived a life.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.439
Out there is a lost love.

00:02:57.439 --> 00:03:00.900
He thinks about her sometimes when he sits
down in his workshop and lets his thoughts

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:01.400
drift away.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.969
That's what I think, anyway."

00:03:02.969 --> 00:03:06.959
"The Mandalorian" is set well before the events
of the sequel trilogy, so it's plausible that

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:11.840
Season 3 will reveal more about Babu's life
before he crosses paths with Rey and the gang.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.709
If it's him at all.

